# A build context is copied wholesale to the daemon, whether or not a COPY names
# it. Without this file that is the whole working tree — ~300 MB of installed
# node_modules and the Android sources, none of which the image uses.
#
# The frontend stage installs its dependencies in a layer of its own, so the
# later `COPY frontend/ .` would put the developer's node_modules straight back
# on top of it: the image would ship whatever they happened to have. CI never saw
# it, building from a clean checkout. pnpm makes it a hard failure rather than a
# wasted layer, because its node_modules is a tree of symlinks into
# node_modules/.pnpm that does not survive being copied out of context.
target/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

# Not part of any image.
android/
.git/
result
result-*
